    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1137">

                <pb facs="1057" n="799" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg799"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111E1 1/15</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bernstorff</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">J. Nr. A 5149]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cedarhurst, N. Y.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 18, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 21</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: In continuation of my
                    note of the 17th Ultimo<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1137-f1"/> have the honor to draw
                    your excellency’s kind attention to the enclosed clipping from the New York <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Herald</hi> of the 14th instant.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1137-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>According to this article speed boats are being built in large numbers by the
                    Greenport Basin and Construction Company of Greenport, New York, apparently for
                    a belligerent power; it is said they are to be used in destroying
                    submarines.</p>
                <p>Four boats are said to be already completed and waiting to be taken and carried
                    away.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Bernstorff</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
